Are you a hands-on person who enjoys working in a dynamic logistics environment? For our location in Eindhoven, we are looking for an enthusiastic Warehouse Employee.

As a Warehouse Employee, you will help ensure that the logistics process runs smoothly. Your responsibilities will include receiving, checking, storing and shipping goods. Together with your colleagues, you will make sure that everything is in the right place and that orders are processed on time.

What are we looking for?

- You are available to work full-time; 2 shifts
- You are accurate, reliable and responsible;
- You have a proactive and flexible attitude;
- Previous warehouse experience is a plus, but not required;
- You have a good command of the English language;
- A forklift or reach truck certificate is a plus;
- You are a real team player and are not afraid to roll up your sleeves.

We are looking for a talented and ambitious Sous Chef to join our team. In this versatile position, you will be responsible for the day-to-day running of the kitchen, managing the kitchen team and working with our Chef to improve our offer and work process. The challenge in this position is to keep an overview of our various catering outlets; the breakfast restaurant and banqueting rooms for meetings and events. These different catering concepts require a different approach and preparation, so there is a lot of variety in the tasks and every day is different.This is what you like to do:
• You are responsible for the overview, planning and preparation of our various catering outlets.
• You manage the kitchen team, in the absence of the Chef you are responsible for the entire kitchen.
• Working from our Inntel Hotels menu: Inntel Originals.
• You support with orders, making schedules and possibly recruiting and selecting new colleagues.
• You work daily according to HAACP guidelines and ensure a clean working environment.

